            <ArticleTitle>Functional airway obstruction observed with hyperpolarized 129 Xenon-MRI.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/1754-9485.12660</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hyperpolarized 129 Xenon-MRI (HP 129 Xe MRI) is an emerging imaging modality that allows assessment of both ventilation and gas transfer. Most research to date has focused on non-malignant pulmonary diseases. However, the capability of evaluating the two primary physiological processes of the lung (ventilation and gas transfer) makes HP 129 Xe MRI a promising imaging modality in the management of patients with lung cancer.</AbstractText>
